    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0184" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg134"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received February 28, 1894.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1784.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of a communication sent by me to the Tsung-li-Yamên, asking that a proclamation
                    be issued reprobating the practice of counterfeiting or fraudulently imitating
                    trade-marks on American piece goods, and directing all officials to arrest and
                    punish all persons who are found guilty of this offense.</p>
                <p>I have etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>




